    "extracted text": "The paper focuses on Al-Cu 206 cast alloys with varying iron contents (0.15-0.5 wt%) and different levels of Mn and Si. The AA designation is 206.0 or A206.0. The study examines the effect of iron-rich intermetallics on tensile properties under T4 (solution and natural aging) and T7 (solution and artificial overaging) conditions. T4 treatment involves solution treatment at 505°C (941°F) for 2h, 520°C (968°F) for 2h, 525°C (977°F) for 8h, then water quench at 65°C (149°F), followed by natural aging at room temperature for 7 days. T7 treatment has the same solution treatment followed by artificial aging at 185°C (365°F) for 5h. The study designates alloys based on approximate Fe, Si, and Mn content - first digit represents Fe content (B for baseline at max 0.15% Fe), second digit for Si content, and third digit for Mn content.",
    
    "property mapping": "- UTS (MPa) = Ultimate Tensile Strength in Megapascals
- YS (MPa) = Yield Strength at 0.2% offset strain in Megapascals
- El (pct) = Elongation percentage
- T4 = Solution treatment and natural aging
- T7 = Solution treatment and artificial overaging",
    
    "abbreviations": "- bal = balance (remainder aluminum)
- T4 = Solution treatment (505°C for 2h, 520°C for 2h, 525°C for 8h, water quench at 65°C) followed by natural aging at room temperature for 7 days
- T7 = Solution treatment (same as T4) followed by artificial aging at 185°C for 5h
- In alloy designation XXX: first digit = approximate Fe content (B for baseline at 0.15% Fe max), second digit = Si content, third digit = Mn content",
    
